From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] OPENBOOK: arm64: record what heavy translations embed,
 through the optimizer

Step P1b of the persistent translation cache (ANAL-381), on patch 10.
Heavy translations embed the same kinds of absolute operands as lite ones,
but guest addresses pass through MachineIR and its folding passes before
they reach the code. This keeps each address's provenance through the
optimizer, or marks the region not persistable, without changing what is
generated.

- MachineInsnX86_64 carries what its immediate refers to: a kind and a
  32-bit aux, in what was padding, so instructions don't grow. For an
  address, aux is a pending left shift (0 for the address itself); for a
  heap resource, it's (offset << 8) | id. Copies keep it.
- The heavy frontend tags ADR/ADRP, literal addresses, the BL/BLR link
  value (through the semantics player), its URECPE/URSQRTE tables and the
  LD2-LD4/ST2-ST4 permutation masks (new resource ids 3-5,
  GetHeavyHostResource).
- FoldInsns keeps a record only when the folded value is still that address
  plus a constant: a 64-bit add or subtract of a number, a mask clearing at
  most the low 12 bits, and the TBI masking pair (shl 8, then shr 8, which
  gives the address back). It looks each definition up once. Any other fold
  of an address still happens, so code doesn't change, but marks the
  MachineIR, and GenCode the MachineCode, not persistable. An address is
  never narrowed into a 32-bit immediate operand; that only fits below
  4 GiB.
- Emission: a tagged MovqRegImm goes out through MovqPersistent (the same
  bytes above 4 GiB); PseudoJump's exits and the recovery labels use
  MovqGuestAddr.
- SymbolizeTranslation refuses a not-persistable translation and resolves
  resources from both tiers with an offset.

Tests: the fixture list adds 15 heavy cases (every heavy operand kind,
ADRP+ADD folded, EOR and a 32-bit add on an address that must be refused,
LD3/ST3), run through the same scan, in-process and second-process
differentials and omission checks; the region corpus test takes
BERBERIS_RELOC_TIER=heavy. DigitalisBench.DISABLED_TranslateRegionCorpus
gets a heavy tier and an interleaved determinism check.

Co-authored-by: multica-agent <github@multica.ai>
